        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(cron): skip heartbeat-enabled checks for cron-sourced main-session wakes (#101537)",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nCron jobs with `sessionTarget: \"main\"` that deliver systemEvent payloads are skipped with `status: \"skipped\", error: \"disabled\"` when the main agent doesn't have heartbeat scheduling configured. The cron job fires on schedule but the main session is never woken.\n\nRoot cause: `runHeartbeatOnce` checks `isHeartbeatEnabledForAgent(cfg, agentId)` and `resolveHeartbeatIntervalMs()` before executing. When another agent has heartbeat configured but \"main\" does not, `isHeartbeatEnabledForAgent(cfg, \"main\")` returns false — causing the skip.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nCron jobs manage their own scheduling via `CronService`. The per-agent heartbeat config and interval resolution checks are designed for the heartbeat scheduler, not for cron-sourced wakes. The fix wraps these two checks in `if (opts.source !== \"cron\")` so cron-sourced runs bypass them while still respecting the global `areHeartbeatsEnabled()` toggle.\n\n## User Impact\n\n- Cron jobs with `sessionTarget: \"main\"` now work correctly even when the main agent doesn't have heartbeat scheduling configured\n- The global heartbeat toggle still applies — cron jobs are skipped when heartbeats are globally disabled\n- No change for regular heartbeat scheduling behavior\n\n## Evidence\n\n- 45/45 tests pass in heartbeat-runner.returns-default-unset.test.ts (including 2 new regression tests)\n- Format clean (oxfmt)\n\nFixes #101537\n",
        "branch": "fix/cron-heartbeat-disabled-skip-v2",
